      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=4,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{5}X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{5}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{5}X] & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
